WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:10.163
A JVM with the AOT cache still maps classes, links, interprets, and waits for the JIT.

2
00:00:10.163 --> 00:00:15.023
In Quarkus's benchmark, its first request took 1,859 ms.

3
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.223
A native image answered in 581 ms, because it did that work in the build.

4
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:24.427
The native-image builder starts at main.

5
00:00:24.427 --> 00:00:31.071
It follows every method call and field access it can see, and works out which classes can show up at each call.

6
00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:36.799
Code it never reaches is left out, and so are the JDK classes nothing uses.

7
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.166
It runs static initializers where it can, and saves their objects in the image heap.

8
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:47.611
Then it compiles every reachable method to machine code.

9
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:53.686
The binary needs no class loading, no bytecode verification, no interpreter and no JIT.

10
00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:59.909
This is the closed-world assumption: everything the program will run is known at build time.

11
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:09.261
The price is what the analysis can't see: reflection, proxies, resources loaded by name, JNI and serialization.

12
00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:11.211
Constants are fine.

13
00:01:11.211 --> 00:01:16.188
Class.forName with a literal name just works, because the build can read it.

14
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.337
But this decoder takes the class name from a Kafka message header.

15
00:01:20.337 --> 00:01:21.768
The build can't know it.

16
00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:29.303
On the JVM, Class.forName finds PaymentAuthorized on the class path and loads it.

17
00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:31.929
The native binary can't load classes.

18
00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:38.469
Nobody told the build about PaymentAuthorized, so the call throws MissingReflectionRegistrationError.

19
00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:40.412
It's an Error: don't catch it.

20
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.942
You tell the build in reachability-metadata.json, on the class path.

21
00:01:45.942 --> 00:01:49.697
An entry names the type and the members your code uses.

22
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.822
A constructor is called &lt;init&gt;.

23
00:01:51.822 --> 00:01:57.465
Parameter types are fully qualified, and every method lists them, even when there are none.

24
00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:02.153
The condition turns the entry on only once EventDecoder is reached.

25
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.438
Now PaymentAuthorized decodes as it did on the JVM.

26
00:02:07.438 --> 00:02:10.824
RefundIssued isn't listed, so it still fails.

27
00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.922
In a Quarkus app you rarely write this file.

28
00:02:13.922 --> 00:02:19.173
Extensions know what their libraries reflect on, and Quarkus generates the JSON.

29
00:02:19.173 --> 00:02:23.768
For classes only your code knows about, you add RegisterForReflection.
